A note on provenance, since the question is reasonable
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

These DARs are commonly encountered alongside the OpenZeppelin Canton token
template, which is licensed AGPL-3.0. Ballast takes no code from it.

The interface DARs themselves are Apache-2.0 artifacts published by Digital
Asset, and redistributing them carries no copyleft obligation. The only token
implementation in this repository is ledger/ballast-test/daml/Ballast/Testing/
Registry.daml, which is original work written for this project's test suite and
never ships in the deployed package.

Ballast therefore has no AGPL obligation.
